</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2e00d2e-2da7-11f1-94e9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-87LW4T8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2e00d2e-2da7-11f1-94e9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-87LW4T8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdd09254-8590-11f1-851f-bb981e703a77</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 05:56:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2e00d2e-2da7-11f1-94e9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-87LW4T8.jpg">AFP - SAEED KHAN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Gabon and France deepen industrial cooperation with Eramet manganese deal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260722-gabon-and-france-deepen-industrial-cooperation-with-eramet-manganese-deal</link><description>
French mining group Eramet is considering a major expansion of manganese processing in Gabon under an agreement that could strengthen the country’s industrial base, modernise its railway network and reduce its reliance on exports of unprocessed ore.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5bbb926-8488-11f1-9289-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201639434838.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5bbb926-8488-11f1-9289-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201639434838.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f66a1f82-84f8-11f1-b95b-159cb199153e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 08:52:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5bbb926-8488-11f1-9289-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201639434838.jpg">© Ludovic Marin / Pool AFP via AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Germany looks to Azerbaijan as Armenia ties shift regional relationships</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260722-germany-looks-to-azerbaijan-as-armenia-ties-shift-the-regional-map</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and Azerbaijani President Ilham Aliyev have signed a series of economic agreements aimed at deepening Berlin's access to Baku's gas reserves and transit routes. The deal comes as Germany works to diversify its energy supply, and as Azerbaijan balances a Europe-leaning Armenia against a recently repaired relationship with Moscow.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/419cc27e-8509-11f1-9cd9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2QJ4YJ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/419cc27e-8509-11f1-9cd9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2QJ4YJ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b96ba18a-84e1-11f1-a40b-5172daa12d9e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 05:08:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/419cc27e-8509-11f1-9cd9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2QJ4YJ.jpg">AFP - TOBIAS SCHWARZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France’s emergency agriculture bill passed, amid divisions over pesticides</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260721-france-s-emergency-agriculture-bill-passed-amid-divisions-over-pesticides</link><description>
