</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df361890-5675-11f1-b9ec-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Le-pr%C3%A9sident-zambien-Hakainde-Hichilema-%C3%A0-Harare-au-Zimbabwe-le-14-novembre-2025.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df361890-5675-11f1-b9ec-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Le-pr%C3%A9sident-zambien-Hakainde-Hichilema-%C3%A0-Harare-au-Zimbabwe-le-14-novembre-2025.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">566666c0-7eaf-11f1-8b4b-d7a352c90397</guid><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 11:41:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Melissa Chemam</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Senegal's Faye backs former president Sall's bid for UN top job in U-turn</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260721-senegal-s-faye-backs-ex-president-sall-s-bid-for-un-top-job-in-u-turn</link><description>
Senegalese President Bassirou Diomaye Faye has endorsed former president Macky Sall's candidacy to become the next United Nations secretary-general, the foreign ministry said on Monday, giving his predecessor crucial backing from his home country despite deep political divisions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c655eb0-84c1-11f1-a1d4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-34MQ7N7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c655eb0-84c1-11f1-a1d4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-34MQ7N7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">86f1bada-84d9-11f1-8d9c-db2ffabab7f1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 14:37:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c655eb0-84c1-11f1-a1d4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-34MQ7N7.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Burnham becomes UK's seventh PM in a decade after Starmer resigns</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260720-andy-burnham-becomes-the-uk-seventh-prime-minister-in-a-decade-after-starmer-resigns</link><description>
Prime Minister Andy Burnham said politicians “need to be better” as he delivered his first speech on Monday as the United Kingdom's new leader.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a570e99c-842d-11f1-853d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201407267823.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a570e99c-842d-11f1-853d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201407267823.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8763d836-8439-11f1-9f3e-37d1e99982f8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 13:42:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a570e99c-842d-11f1-853d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201407267823.jpg">© Aaron Chown/Pool PA via AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's Fontainebleau forest faces long recovery after wildfires</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260720-france-s-fontainebleau-forest-faces-long-road-to-recover-after-wildfires</link><description>
The wildfires that ravaged more than 2,000 hectares of the Fontainebleau Forest have destroyed habitats and have put its diversity of plant and animal life under threat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bb247fdc-83c0-11f1-9803-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2CE4J7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bb247fdc-83c0-11f1-9803-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2CE4J7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8aa9afda-841a-11f1-9c6d-5d87d60156c9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 21:31:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bb247fdc-83c0-11f1-9803-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2CE4J7.jpg">AFP - LOU BENOIST</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>France welcomes Gabon's Oligui as mineral and military ties defy African rift</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260720-france-welcomes-gabon-s-oligui-as-mineral-and-military-ties-defy-wider-rift-in-africa</link><description>
Gabon's President Brice Clotaire Oligui Nguema begins a three-day official visit to France on Monday, underlining the close relationship between Paris and one of its few remaining key allies in Francophone Africa. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2310c8f4-c935-11f0-9ff9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-84YX7RL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2310c8f4-c935-11f0-9ff9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-84YX7RL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f5973582-8420-11f1-b83a-7d8e98d13a62</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:58:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2310c8f4-c935-11f0-9ff9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-84YX7RL.jpg">AFP - LUDOVIC MARIN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ecowas appoints Senegal's Birame Diop to drive regional reforms</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260720-ecowas-appoints-senegal-s-birame-diop-to-drive-regional-reforms</link><description>
West African leaders have appointed Senegal's former defence minister, General Birame Diop, to lead the Economic Community of West African States Commission, placing a military figure with extensive United Nations peacekeeping experience at the helm as the bloc seeks to recover from the departure of three member states.
